{"audio": "romans-10.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 147467, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1467, "text": "Romans, Chapter Ten."}, {"start_ms": 1467, "end_ms": 7067, "text": "Brethren, my heart's desire and prayer to God for Israel is, that they might be saved."}, {"start_ms": 7067, "end_ms": 11600, "text": "For I bear them record that they have a zeal of God, but not according to knowledge."}, {"start_ms": 11600, "end_ms": 20267, "text": "For they being ignorant of God's righteousness, and going about to establish their own righteousness, have not submitted themselves unto the righteousness of God."}, {"start_ms": 20267, "end_ms": 24667, "text": "For Christ is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth."}, {"start_ms": 24667, "end_ms": 31333, "text": "For Moses describeth the righteousness which is of the law, That the man which doeth those things shall live by them."}, {"start_ms": 31333, "end_ms": 38800, "text": "But the righteousness which is of faith speaketh on this wise, Say not in thine heart, Who shall ascend into heaven?"}, {"start_ms": 38800, "end_ms": 44533, "text": "(that is, to bring Christ down from above:) Or, Who shall descend into the deep?"}, {"start_ms": 44533, "end_ms": 49467, "text": "(that is, to bring up Christ again from the dead.) But what saith it?"}, {"start_ms": 49467, "end_ms": 63733, "text": "The word is nigh thee, even in thy mouth, and in thy heart: that is, the word of faith, which we preach; That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved."}, {"start_ms": 63733, "end_ms": 69867, "text": "For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation."}, {"start_ms": 69867, "end_ms": 74133, "text": "For the scripture saith, Whosoever believeth on him shall not be ashamed."}, {"start_ms": 74133, "end_ms": 82000, "text": "For there is no difference between the Jew and the Greek: for the same Lord over all is rich unto all that call upon him."}, {"start_ms": 82000, "end_ms": 86133, "text": "For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved."}, {"start_ms": 86133, "end_ms": 89600, "text": "How then shall they call on him in whom they have not believed?"}, {"start_ms": 89600, "end_ms": 93200, "text": "and how shall they believe in him of whom they have not heard?"}, {"start_ms": 93200, "end_ms": 95600, "text": "and how shall they hear without a preacher?"}, {"start_ms": 95600, "end_ms": 98400, "text": "And how shall they preach, except they be sent?"}, {"start_ms": 98400, "end_ms": 105067, "text": "as it is written, How beautiful are the feet of them that preach the gospel of peace, and bring glad tidings of good things!"}, {"start_ms": 105067, "end_ms": 107467, "text": "But they have not all obeyed the gospel."}, {"start_ms": 107467, "end_ms": 111333, "text": "For Esaias saith, Lord, who hath believed our report?"}, {"start_ms": 111333, "end_ms": 115333, "text": "So then faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of God."}, {"start_ms": 115333, "end_ms": 117333, "text": "But I say, Have they not heard?"}, {"start_ms": 117333, "end_ms": 122400, "text": "Yes verily, their sound went into all the earth, and their words unto the ends of the world."}, {"start_ms": 122400, "end_ms": 125200, "text": "But I say, Did not Israel know?"}, {"start_ms": 125200, "end_ms": 133067, "text": "First Moses saith, I will provoke you to jealousy by them that are no people, and by a foolish nation I will anger you."}, {"start_ms": 133067, "end_ms": 140400, "text": "But Esaias is very bold, and saith, I was found of them that sought me not; I was made manifest unto them that asked not after me."}, {"start_ms": 140400, "end_ms": 147467, "text": "But to Israel he saith, All day long I have stretched forth my hands unto a disobedient and gainsaying people."}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 80, "e": 543, "si": 0}, {"t":